1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,380
Could a yeti really survive in

2
00:00:01,380 --> 00:00:02,390
the Himalayas?

3
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:04,390
Let's build one.

4
00:00:04,427 --> 00:00:06,667
In Sherpa and Tibetan stories,

5
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:07,573
it's a huge,

6
00:00:07,573 --> 00:00:09,590
hairy walker of the high snow.

7
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:11,408
But a big body sinks in

8
00:00:11,408 --> 00:00:12,230
deep snow.

9
00:00:12,267 --> 00:00:13,747
So you grow wide,

10
00:00:13,747 --> 00:00:14,592
furry feet,

11
00:00:14,592 --> 00:00:15,968
like a snowshoe hare.

12
00:00:15,968 --> 00:00:17,413
They spread your weight,

13
00:00:17,413 --> 00:00:18,550
so you stay on top.

14
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,160
But the air up here is

15
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:20,710
thin.

16
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,340
So you tune your body for

17
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:23,392
low oxygen,

18
00:00:23,392 --> 00:00:24,160
like the yak,

19
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:25,822
whose genes are built for high

20
00:00:25,822 --> 00:00:26,630
altitude.

21
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:28,280
But then winter comes,

22
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:29,510
and there's nothing to eat.

23
00:00:29,547 --> 00:00:30,848
So you sleep through it,

24
00:00:30,848 --> 00:00:32,206
like a brown bear,

25
00:00:32,206 --> 00:00:34,470
living on stored fat for months.

26
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,710
Now look at what you built.

27
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:37,920
A big,

28
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:39,270
furry bear.

29
00:00:39,493 --> 00:00:41,498
In twenty seventeen,

30
00:00:41,498 --> 00:00:44,040
scientists tested nine yeti samples.

31
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:45,220
One was a dog.

32
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:47,350
The other eight were Asian bears.

33
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:49,100
And the name yeti comes from

34
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:51,333
Tibetan words meaning rock bear.

35
00:00:51,333 --> 00:00:52,907
So the legend isn't empty.

36
00:00:52,907 --> 00:00:55,030
It grew from a real animal.

